# Environment variables for StenRAG
#
# This file is loaded AUTOMATICALLY by `src/llm_client.py` (on the first
# `make_client()` call).  You do NOT need to export anything by hand.
#
# A real environment variable ALWAYS wins over this file, so you can
# still override a value for a single run:
#
#   $env:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY = "sk-..."; python eval/quick20_eval.py
#
# NEVER commit the real .env — it is already in .gitignore.

# ── DeepSeek (hosted, recommended for the eval harness) ───────────────────
# Obtain from https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-your-deepseek-key-here

# ── OpenAI (alternative to DeepSeek) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Used by src/llm_client.py when DEEPSEEK_API_KEY is not set.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-key-here

# ── Local self-hosted LLM (vLLM / Ollama) ─────────────────────────────────
# When STENRAG_LLM_BASE_URL is set, the local server is targeted INSTEAD
# of the hosted API, and no real API key is needed (vLLM ignores the
# bearer token unless it was started with --api-key).
#
# STENRAG_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8013/v1
# STENRAG_LLM_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b
# STENRAG_LLM_API_KEY=          # only if the server enforces auth
#
# See src/local_llm_server.py for the weight lookup / auto-start logic.
